Z||000030||87GTZ34||06-26-2001||08:40 AM||||Aus, I was away a couple of days and just saw this.  Sorry to hear you were under the weather.  Sounds serious.  I hope you are all better now.  I also suffer from a rare one that wipes me from time to time... Its called Fieroitus.  I worked until 5am one night/morning and 3am another recently.  I said to myself I have to quit, I'm getting too old for all-nighters (at least car related ones anyway).  I'm no doctor (but I play one on the PFF... old US joke), but take it easy and don't work so hard.  Work is like a devoted dog... somehow the work always seems to wait for you to return.<P>P.S. to Cliff, the spellchecker needs an adjustment... I won't say what it returned for 'Aus'.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Sage||06-26-2001||12:25 PM||||Sorry to hear that you were down.  Glad to hear that you are back and getting into full swing.  Being down does have a way of altering your perspective.  Follow your heart, it knows the way home.<P>Don't over do, get rested up, and speak up if you need help laying up parts!<P>Take care, and have a good one.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
